within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L04A_Immunosuppressants.L04AA24_Abatacept;
model Abatacept_Li2019_PD_das28
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Li_2019 :: DAS28 (Disease Activity Score in 28 joints)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 6.22,      // [1]
    Emax = -2.15,  // [1]
    EC50 = 0.00682,  // [kg/m3; μg/mL × 0.001]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 μg/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 69, Interval = 0.138),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Abatacept_Li2019_PD_das28</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Li X et al., <i>Journal of clinical pharmacology 59(2):245–257</i> 2019 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcph.1308\">doi:10.1002/jcph.1308</a>) — Disease Activity Score in 28 joints against abatacept μg/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       6.22          drug-free response (baseline) (E0, Q324)
  Emax  =       2.15          maximal effect term (Emax,aba, Q323)
  EC50  =       6.82 μg/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one μg/mL of abatacept per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 6.22   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (6.82 μg/mL)  response 5.145
  exposure -> infinity  response 4.07</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Li_2019: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Abatacept_Li2019_PD_das28;
